  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a topic page with one odd message block to show its other messages, as legacy did and as our list parsers already do, so that one block does not turn a page into an error.\n\n### Scenario\nA page with one `messagetable` block lacking its `t<n>` anchor, its `s2` cell or its `para` div: `MessageBlockParser.extract` throws `missingElement` for the page, and the reader shows an error. The deleted-post wrapper `messagetabledel` is still pending capture (#123, `docs/lots/LOT-030-message-blocks.md:47,90`), so the shape of the block most likely to hit this is unknown. No capture shows a failing page today.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRParsing/Topic/MessageBlockParser.swift:29-33`: in the loop, `guard let author = try author(in: elements) else { continue }`, then `let numreponse = try numreponse(in: elements)` and `let content = try content(in: elements, numreponse: numreponse)`: each throws for the page.\n- `MessageActionsParser.actions(in:)` and `MPStoragePageParser.firstMessage` inherit it through `extract`.\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRParsing/TopicList/TopicListParser.swift:49-57`: an unreadable row is skipped; the page is malformed only when all rows fail (LESSONS 44).\n- Legacy is nil-tolerant per message: `ParseMessagesOperation.m:139-177` @ `87fe0d1c`.\n\n### Fix\nSkip a block that cannot be read; throw only when the page has `messagetable` elements and none is readable; keep the skipped count for diagnostics. Do not hand-build the deleted-post placeholder: #123 captures it.\n\n### Tests (first one fails before the fix)\n`MessageBlockParserTests.skipsUnreadableBlock`: an `R20` capture with the anchor removed from one block gives N-1 blocks in order (today `missingElement`); a second case with every block broken still throws.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
