   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-verified at `dev-swift` @ `fa96c1c1`: `MessageBlockParser.extract` still throws for the whole page when one `messagetable` block lacks its `s2` cell, its `t<n>` anchor or its `para` div. Legacy reads each message on its own with nil fields (`HFRswift/Wrapped/ParseMessagesOperation.m:139-177` @ `87fe0d1c`).\n\nPlan:\n- `extract` skips a block it cannot read and keeps the skipped count and the first failure (internal `Extraction`); the page throws only when it has blocks and none is readable (LESSONS 44). Ads still skipped as before.\n- `MessageActionsParser` stays aligned (same `extract`). `MPStoragePageParser.firstMessage` refuses a page whose **first** block was skipped (it edits the first message: the next one must never pass for the document).\n- No hand-built deleted-post block (#123 captures it).\n- Tests first, on the `R20` capture mutated in memory: one block without its anchor / `s2` / `para` → N-1 blocks in order; every block broken → throws; MPStorage with its first block broken → `unreadablePage`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
